{"id":"G2020","lemma":"ἐπιφώσκω","transliteration":"epiphōskō","sayIt":"epiphōskō","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to dawn","meaning":"ἐπι-φώσκω\n[in LXX for הָלַל hi., Job.41:18 A (Βא, ἐπιφαύσκ-) * ;]\n1. to let shine.\n2. to dawn (cf. MM, Exp., xiv): Luk.23:54; before εἰς, Mat_28:1.†\n(AS)","glosses":["dawn","beginning"],"count":2,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-28","v":1,"renderings":{"bsb":"at dawn","kjv":"as it began to dawn"}},{"chapterId":"luk-23","v":54,"renderings":{"bsb":"was beginning"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Matthew 28:1","note":"Now after the Sabbath, as it began to dawn on the first day of the week, Mary Magdalene and the other Mary came to see the tomb.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Luke 23:54","note":"It was the day of the Preparation, and the Sabbath was drawing near.","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"G20200","lemma":"γόος","transliteration":"goos","gloss":"for"},{"id":"G20201","lemma":"δᾳδουχία","transliteration":"dadouchia","gloss":"torch-bearing"},{"id":"G20202","lemma":"δακτυλήθρα","transliteration":"daktulēthra","gloss":"thumb-screw"},{"id":"G20203","lemma":"δανίζω","transliteration":"danizō","gloss":"to lend/borrow"},{"id":"G20204","lemma":"δειλανδρέω","transliteration":"deilandreō","gloss":"be cowardly"},{"id":"G20205","lemma":"δειλόομαι","transliteration":"deiloomai","gloss":"be afraid"},{"id":"G20206","lemma":"δειλόψυχος","transliteration":"deilopsuchos","gloss":"fainthearted"},{"id":"G20207","lemma":"δεινάζω","transliteration":"deinazō","gloss":"be in straits"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}